@startuml
title Appendix — Random Forest inference foundation
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 230

rectangle "Explicit selection\nRANDOM_FOREST" as selection
rectangle "CustomerSnapshot\nactivities only" as snapshot
rectangle "Four bounded features\nvolume · crypto ratio\ncross-border ratio · incomplete ratio" as features
rectangle "Packaged inputs\nTribuo protobuf + canonical manifest" as artifact
rectangle "Lazy runtime\nload once + memoize" as runtime
rectangle "Fail-closed validation\ntrust anchors · domains · uniform weights\ntrees · hyperparameters · provenance" as validation
rectangle "Fixed weighted ensemble\n31 trees · request-time inference only" as forest
rectangle "REVIEW_ELEVATED vote share\n+ predicted class + provenance" as output

snapshot --> features
selection --> runtime
artifact --> runtime
runtime --> validation
validation --> forest
features --> forest
forest --> output

note bottom of forest
Example: 22 / 31 uniformly weighted trees
vote REVIEW_ELEVATED -> score ~= 0.710.
This is a vote share, not a calibrated probability.
end note

note bottom of output
Packaged and selectable, but trained on
12 hand-authored synthetic rows.
#130: existing fixture cannot support a
defensible performance/Bayes-error benchmark.
end note

rectangle "Bounded observation window\nminimum 12" as window
rectangle "Pinned 12-row feature reference" as reference
rectangle "Per-feature two-sample KS D\nmax D >= 0.50 -> REVIEW_TRIGGERED" as drift
rectangle "Descriptive drift report\nobservability only" as report

window --> drift : same four features
reference --> drift
drift --> report

note bottom of report
Input-shift review trigger only.
No concept/performance/calibration/AML claim.
end note
@enduml
